    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d524-a1">

                <pb facs="0816" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg688"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 310.–Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Elduayen to Mr. Reed</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry of
                            State</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName type="venue"><hi rendition="#italic">Palace</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1885-02-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 19, 1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: Having given account to my
                    colleague, the minister of ultramar, of the note which you were pleased to
                    address me on the 8th of December last, he informs me that it has been recently
                    decided that, when it is shown to the satisfaction of the treasury officers of
                    the provinces of ultramar that the fault in a manifest is only due to an error
                    in translation, the captains of vessels will not incur a fine or any
                    responsibility.</p>
                <p>I avail, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. ELDUAYEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
